)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation."] [:db/add "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3 x}\\cdot 3 \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{5}{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}3 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3}{e^{\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [:db/add "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/answer-fields "ce88c0d7-692b-5115-9ff0-7a3fad5b60fe"] [:db/add "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/answer-fields "3495b22a-5a40-5f4c-a29c-2521e744ca38"] [:db/add "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/answer-fields "70375abd-6d28-58de-b77f-ce69697a327a"] [:db/ensure "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/questions "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "ae7dd269-edc9-551c-acaa-27f2d1522632"] [:db/add "generator" :questi